  "query_preview": "..FOR EXTREME SOUTHWESTERN CALIFORNIA INCLUDING ORANGE...\nSAN DIEGO...WESTERN RIVERSIDE AND SOUTHWESTERN SAN BERNARDINO\nCOUNTIES...\n\n...UPDATED AVIATION DISCUSSION...\n\nHigh pressure continues to dominate aloft but has shifted just far \nenough east to bring some monsoonal moisture over the area through \nthe afternoon. Light rain has been observed from the San Diego coast \ninto the San Diego mountains with accumulations less than 0.1 \ninches. Rain and storm chances will continue through this afternoon \nwith the highest chances in the mountains and the San Diego deserts. \nConditions will dry out by this evening, leaving chances for rain \nbelow 5% through the end of the week. \n\nHigh temperatures will stay slightly cooler through Wednesday as the \nupper level ridge stays a little east. Heat is expected to return \nThursday through the end of the week as high pressure aloft builds \nand expands west once again. High temperatures will warm to be 10-15 \ndegrees above the seasonal average by Friday and into the weekend.",
